#: src/extensions/languages.md:211
msgid ""
"The `injections.scm` file defines rules for embedding one language within "
"another, such as code blocks in Markdown or SQL queries in Python strings."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:213
msgid "Here's an example from an `injections.scm` file for Markdown:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:215
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"(fenced_code_block\n"
"  (info_string\n"
"    (language) @injection.language)\n"
"  (code_fence_content) @injection.content)\n"
"\n"
"((inline) @content\n"
" (#set! injection.language \"markdown-inline\"))\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:225
msgid ""
"This query identifies fenced code blocks, capturing the language specified "
"in the info string and the content within the block. It also captures inline "
"content and sets its language to \"markdown-inline\"."
msgstr ""

