#: src/extensions/languages.md:298
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:300
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"; include only the content of the method in the function\n"
"(method_definition\n"
"    body: (_\n"
"        \"{\"\n"
"        (_)* @function.inside\n"
"        \"}\")) @function.around\n"
"\n"
"; match function.around for declarations with no body\n"
"(function_signature_item) @function.around\n"
"\n"
"; join all adjacent comments into one\n"
"(comment)+ @comment.around\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:317
msgid ""
"The `redactions.scm` file defines text redaction rules. When collaborating "
"and sharing your screen, it makes sure that certain syntax nodes are "
"rendered in a redacted mode to avoid them from leaking."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:319
msgid "Here's an example from a `redactions.scm` file for JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:328
msgid ""
"This query marks number and string values in key-value pairs and arrays for "
"redaction."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:332
msgid "@redact"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:332
msgid "Captures values to be redacted"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:336
msgid "The `runnables.scm` file defines rules for detecting runnable code."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:338
msgid "Here's an example from a `runnables.scm` file for JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:340
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"(\n"
"    (document\n"
"        (object\n"
"            (pair\n"
"                key: (string\n"
"                    (string_content) @_name\n"
"                    (#eq? @_name \"scripts\")\n"
"                )\n"
"                value: (object\n"
"                    (pair\n"
"                        key: (string (string_content) @run @script)\n"
"                    )\n"
"                )\n"
"            )\n"
"        )\n"
"    )\n"
"    (#set! tag package-script)\n"
"    (#set! tag composer-script)\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:362
msgid ""
"This query detects runnable scripts in package.json and composer.json files."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:364
msgid ""
"The `@run` capture specifies where the run button should appear in the "
"editor. Other captures, except those prefixed with an underscore, are "
"exposed as environment variables with a prefix of "
"`ZED_CUSTOM_$(capture_name)` when running the code."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:368
msgid "@\\_name"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:368
msgid "Captures the \"scripts\" key"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:369
msgid "@run"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:369
msgid "Captures the script name"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:370
msgid "@script"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:370
msgid "Also captures the script name (for different purposes)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:376
msgid "Language Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:378
msgid ""
"Zed uses the [Language Server Protocol](https://microsoft.github.io/language-"
"server-protocol/) to provide advanced language support."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:380
msgid ""
"An extension may provide any number of language servers. To provide a "
"language server from your extension, add an entry to your `extension.toml` "
"with the name of your language server and the language(s) it applies to. The "
"entry in the list of `languages` has to match the `name` field from the "
"`config.toml` file for that language:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:382
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[language_servers.my-language-server]\n"
"name = \"My Language LSP\"\n"
"languages = [\"My Language\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:388
msgid ""
"Then, in the Rust code for your extension, implement the "
"`language_server_command` method on your extension:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:406
msgid ""
"You can customize the handling of the language server using several optional "
"methods in the `Extension` trait. For example, you can control how "
"completions are styled using the `label_for_completion` method. For a "
"complete list of methods, see the [API docs for the Zed extension API]"
"(https://docs.rs/zed_extension_api)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:408
msgid "Syntax Highlighting with Semantic Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:410
msgid ""
"Zed supports syntax highlighting using semantic tokens from the attached "
"language servers. This is currently disabled by default, but can be enabled "
"in your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:414
msgid ""
"// Enable semantic tokens globally, backin with tree-sitter highlights for "
"each language:\n"
"  \"semantic_tokens\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:415
msgid "\"combined\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:416
msgid ""
"// Or, specify per-language:\n"
"  \"languages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:418
msgid "\"Rust\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:419
msgid ""
"// No tree-sitter, only LSP semantic tokens:\n"
"      \"semantic_tokens\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:420
msgid "\"full\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:426
msgid "The `semantic_tokens` setting accepts the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:428
msgid ""
"`\"off\"` (default): Do not request semantic tokens from language servers."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:429
msgid ""
"`\"combined\"`: Use LSP semantic tokens together with tree-sitter "
"highlighting."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:430
msgid ""
"`\"full\"`: Use LSP semantic tokens exclusively, replacing tree-sitter "
"highlighting."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:432
msgid "Customizing Semantic Token Styles"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:434
msgid ""
"Zed supports customizing the styles used for semantic tokens. You can define "
"rules in your settings file, which customize how semantic tokens get mapped "
"to styles in your theme."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:438
msgid "\"global_lsp_settings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:439
msgid "\"semantic_token_rules\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:441
msgid ""
"// Highlight macros as keywords.\n"
"        \"token_type\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:442
msgid "\"macro\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:443
msgid "\"style\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:443
msgid "\"syntax.keyword\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:446
msgid ""
"// Highlight unresolved references in bold red.\n"
"        \"token_type\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:447
msgid "\"unresolvedReference\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:448
msgid "\"foreground_color\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:448
msgid "\"#c93f3f\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:449
msgid "\"font_weight\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:449
msgid "\"bold\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:452
msgid ""
"// Underline all mutable variables/references/etc.\n"
"        \"token_modifiers\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:453
msgid "\"mutable\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:454
msgid "\"underline\""
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:461
msgid ""
"All rules that match a given `token_type` and `token_modifiers` are applied. "
"Earlier rules take precedence. If no rules match, the token is not "
"highlighted. User-defined rules take priority over the default rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:463
msgid "Each rule in the `semantic_token_rules` array is defined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:465
msgid ""
"`token_type`: The semantic token type as defined by the [LSP specification]"
"(https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/"
"lsp/3.17/specification/#textDocument_semanticTokens). If omitted, the rule "
"matches all token types."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:466
msgid ""
"`token_modifiers`: A list of semantic token modifiers to match. All "
"modifiers must be present to match."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:467
msgid ""
"`style`: A list of styles from the current syntax theme to use. The first "
"style found is used. Any settings below override that style."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:468
msgid ""
"`foreground_color`: The foreground color to use for the token type, in hex "
"format (e.g., `\"#ff0000\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:469
msgid ""
"`background_color`: The background color to use for the token type, in hex "
"format (e.g., `\"#ff0000\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:470
msgid ""
"`underline`: A boolean or color to underline with, in hex format. If `true`, "
"then the token will be underlined with the text color."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:471
msgid ""
"`strikethrough`: A boolean or color to strikethrough with, in hex format. If "
"`true`, then the token have a strikethrough with the text color."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:472
msgid "`font_weight`: One of `\"normal\"`, `\"bold\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:473
msgid "`font_style`: One of `\"normal\"`, `\"italic\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:475
msgid "Multi-Language Support"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:477
msgid ""
"If your language server supports additional languages, you can use "
"`language_ids` to map Zed `languages` to the desired [LSP-specific "
"`languageId`](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/"
"specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#textDocumentItem) identifiers:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:479
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"\n"
"[language-servers.my-language-server]\n"
"name = \"Whatever LSP\"\n"
"languages = [\"JavaScript\", \"HTML\", \"CSS\"]\n"
"\n"
"[language-servers.my-language-server.language_ids]\n"
"\"JavaScript\" = \"javascript\"\n"
"\"TSX\" = \"typescriptreact\"\n"
"\"HTML\" = \"html\"\n"
"\"CSS\" = \"css\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
